# Brand System Compliance

`docs/brand-system.html` is the **canonical visual reference** for SpokenLeaf UI — color/typography tokens, component demos, spacing & shape, recording flows, marketing accents, and voice/tone examples.

## Before shipping UI

1. **Find the pattern** — Read the matching section in `docs/brand-system.html` (foundation: Logo, Color, Typography, Spacing & Shape; product UI: **Components** — e.g. Recording setup, Recording controls, Note editor recording, Audio playback, Buttons, Status indicators).
2. **Implement from tokens** — Map demo styles to Tailwind/theme tokens (Moss, Slate-blue, Bone, semantic). Reuse `@/lib/brand-styles.ts` (`brandRecordingDot`, `brandTouchTarget`, `brandStatusPill`, `brandCard`, etc.) before inventing new class strings. No orphan hex values.
3. **Match semantics** — Moss = tasks/growth; slate-blue = conversation/info; destructive = active recording/stop. Copy follows **Voice & Tone** (sentence case, no emoji, no exclamation marks).
4. **Dark mode** — Verify against the `.dark` tokens in brand-system (“Moonlit Greenhouse”).

## New or materially changed patterns

If no demo covers what you are building:

1. Design within existing tokens and spacing/shape rules first.
2. **Add a demo card** to the appropriate section in `docs/brand-system.html` in the **same change** (Components for app UI; Marketing Accents for `marketing/`). Include title, short description, and key states/variants.
3. Hoist repeated Tailwind into `lib/brand-styles.ts` when reused (see `css-style-reuse.mdc`).

`docs/BRAND_GUIDELINES.md` is supplementary narrative/positioning; **brand-system wins** for visual specs and component structure.

## Do not

- Ship UI that diverges from an existing brand-system demo without updating the doc.
- Introduce one-off colors, radii, or shadows outside the token system.
